WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.567
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.701
You're here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.033
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:06.367
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:07.334
Thank you for being here.

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:08.434
Guys, it's that time of year.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.133
Tomorrow is SantaCon...

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:11.567
[ Audience laughs, groans ]

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:13.567
...here in New York City.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:14.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.167
You already know what it is.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:19.100
Yeah, at SantaCon, thousands of
people will dress up as Santa

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.534
and pack the streets
for an all-day bar crawl.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.200
So, before you go to bed,
make sure you put out

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.868
a plate of Advil
and a tall glass of Pedialyte.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:29.767
That's right, happy SantaCon.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.701
To everyone in their 20s,
have fun.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:34.567
To everyone in their 30s,
it's getting kind of sad.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.667
Hey, get this,
according to a new survey,

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.968
30% of Americans
have injured themselves

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.868
during holiday-related
activities.

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:45.934
While the other 70% are the ones
filming it for TikTok.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.767
That's right, 30% get injured.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.434
Who knew climbing a ladder
and hanging lights

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.467
on an icy gutter
could be dangerous?

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:55.801
Actually, the most common injury

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.801
is spraining your face
from fake smiling

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.267
after opening a present.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:02.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.000
"It's a Slanket.
Oh, cool.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.033
I -- I'll google it,
and I love it."

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.701
Speaking of the holidays,
this weekend

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.501
First Lady Jill Biden
will give a tour

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.400
of the White House
holiday decorations

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.200
for an HGTV Christmas special.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.267
Yeah, and after that, stay tuned

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.934
for Melania's
decoration special,

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.634
"The Nightmare
Before Christmas."

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:24.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.968
Let's get to some news.
I saw a new poll

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:27.701
that said President Biden's
approval rating

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.901
is now up to 46%.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.133
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.634
46%, that's pretty much
the blood-alcohol content

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.167
of everyone at SantaCon.

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.968
I like that we're cool
with 46% for a president,

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.000
but if a restaurant
had 2 1/2 stars on Yelp,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.167
we'd call
the health department.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.901
Did you guys see this?
A top adviser

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.100
to Senator Bernie Sanders

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.501
said that if Biden
doesn't run in 2024,

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.267
Sanders will give it
a hard look.

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:52.968
Yeah, people weren't sure
about him

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.767
the last two elections,
but maybe they'll vote for him

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.400
now that he's more mature.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.934
Some more big news
from Washington.

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.734
Today, Senator Kyrsten Sinema
announced

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.634
that she's leaving
the Democratic Party

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.167
and registering
as an Independent.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.067
It's good timing, 'cause
nothing says the holiday season

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.734
like leaving a party early.
Right?

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:13.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.167
Well, listen to this.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.901
I heard that if Putin loses
the war in Ukraine,

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.801
he's going to flee
to South America.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.701
Yeah, and he has his disguise
all planned out.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.100
He's gonna wear a shirt.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:29.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.067
Thank you.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:32.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.133
[ Rim shot ]

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.968
Thank you.

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.667
Some business news --
Apple has a new iMessage feature

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.100
that will alert both users

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.067
if they were being spied on
by a state-sponsored attacker.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.467
Yeah, it's never good seeing

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:45.868
"North Korea
has entered the chat."

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:48.200
And you go...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.467
Some entertainment news.

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.567
I read that the
Miss Universe Pageant is moving

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:55.133
from broadcast TV to streaming
on the Roku Channel.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.200
Yep, and now the winner
of the talent portion

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.501
is whoever can find
the Roku Channel.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.701
When asked how
they felt about it,

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:05.801
a representative for the pageant
said, "World peace."

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.734
Guys, last night in L.A.,

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:10.100
there was a big
video-game award show

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.400
called The Game Awards, okay?

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.667
And they got a pretty huge actor
to present.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.100
Take a look at this.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:18.601
-Please join me in welcoming
to the Game Awards, Al Pacino.

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:23.400
-But, uh, I -- I -- I --

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.334
I'm -- It's hard for me
to see the teleprompter.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:31.601
I don't play
a whole lot of video games.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:35.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.767
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.167
-Wha-- Wha-- What?

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.234
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.901
-It was Pacino's
most challenging role yet,

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:45.534
"guy who wants to be here."

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:46.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.567
I don't know if he
played "Super Mario Bros.,"

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.167
but he definitely
ate a mushroom.

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.167
Once the mushrooms
wear off, he's like,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.100
"Say hello
to my little friend."

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.300
[ Mario shrinking sound ]

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:01.901
Thank you.
I do space work.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.734
-Yeah, wow, space work,
very good.

00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:06.000
-Hey, this is going viral.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.334
A man, who was out kayaking,
saw a great white shark.

00:04:09.334 --> 00:04:11.534
Yeah, and then, when he asked
his friend what he should do,

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:12.968
his friend had
a very interesting response.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:14.667
Watch this.

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.434
-Dude, Danny.

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.400
-Yeah.
-What do I do?

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.467
Holy [bleep]
-Film it.

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.601
-Holy [bleep]

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.133
-Honestly, at that point,

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:33.534
what else can you really do,
I guess?

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:36.534
He was like, "Uh, now slap it
with a tortilla!"

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:37.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:41.033
"Slap the shark
with a tortilla!"

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:43.734
And finally, a puppy was found
after he escaped from his home

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:48.100
in Manhattan and swam across
the Hudson River to New Jersey.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.734
He swam all the way
to New Jersey

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.434
just to get away from SantaCon.

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.033
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.133
Let's go write some
thank-you notes.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.701
Come with me.

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:58.100
-[ Rapping indistinctly ]

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.400
♪♪

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.534
♪ I spit some riffs,
they're so savage ♪

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:06.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.601
-What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:10.167
Miley Cyrus is here
tonight, everybody.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:11.868
-Oh, come on.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:18.234
What?

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:19.601
What?
-I don't know.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:20.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.801
I think I've had enough.
-You're tired of it?

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:24.067
-I think I've had
enough of the beard.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.434
[ Audience groans ]
-No.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:27.434
-No.
-Yeah.

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:28.934
-What?
-I'm getting rid of the beard.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:31.567
-What?
[ Audience shouting ]

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.033
-I just decided.
-No!

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.133
-Tonight?

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.033
[ Audience shouting ]

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.667
-Wow.
They're like animals!

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:38.734
-I've got a shaver.

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.167
Should we do it tonight?

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.834
Can we ask Miley Cyrus if she
wants to shave my beard tonight?

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:45.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.234
She would do it.

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:49.634
I'm ready -- I'm ready to get
rid of it, I think.

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:50.734
-You're sick of it.
-I just --

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.434
I think it's too much beard.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:54.033
It's overtaking me.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.234
-You think that you're becoming
more beard than Jimmy.

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:57.434
-No, no joke, people all --

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:58.934
all people want to know about
is the beard.

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.868
That's -- This is more --

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.167
this is getting more attention
than the show.

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.467
It's taking away from the show.

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:05.467
-Well, your beard's
getting a show on Roku, right?

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:07.000
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, of course.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.234
Yeah, it's got
its own show on Roku, but...

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:11.334
I -- I grew my beard,
and then Quest grew his beard,

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:13.501
then Tariq grew a beard,
then Stro grew a beard.

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:14.901
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:15.968
Mark.

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:17.534
Everyone in The Roots
has a beard.

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:18.834
-I said no.

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:20.167
I said, "Just say no."

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:21.501
[ Light laughter ]
-You said that?

00:06:21.501 --> 00:06:23.067
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:27.367
I think, yeah, I think --
'cause, you know, it's enough.

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:28.300
-That's it.
You're done.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.734
-Let's see if Miley will do it.

00:06:29.734 --> 00:06:31.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:32.868
Want to do it?

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:33.901
I'll do it.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.567
If she's down,
I'll do it tonight.

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.300
I don't care, yeah, I love it.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.100
Guys, today's Friday,
and that's usually

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.667
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:42.567
I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.000
and of course I send out
thank-you notes.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
And I was running a bit behind.

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:47.734
So I thought if you guys
wouldn't mind just --

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:49.167
thank you -- I'd like to write
us some --

00:06:49.167 --> 00:06:51.133
James, give us some thank-you
note writing music, please.

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:53.968
♪♪

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:56.000
-He has, like,
a goatee just to mock you.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.367
-Yeah, that's kind
of weird to me.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:58.968
-He didn't even grow
a whole beard.

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:02.567
-[ Laughs ]
-Wow.

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.000
-He doesn't have a beard,
really.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.634
It's more of a, uh --
-It's like a goatee

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:07.834
or a Van Dyke.
-It's like a --

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:10.501
It's like a Mitch Miller-type
of vibe.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:12.901
-Yeah, exactly.

00:07:12.901 --> 00:07:15.400
[ Laughs ]

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.634
Or a Van Dyke mustache.
-I mean, I can shave this thing.

00:07:17.634 --> 00:07:20.167
I did it, I -- Tariq dared me,
I proved it,

00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:23.701
I, you know, La Schmoove.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:26.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:29.367
-I don't got nothing to prove.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:32.434
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.434 --> 00:07:33.767
-Don't edit that.

00:07:33.767 --> 00:07:37.100
[ Laughter ]
Don't edit.

00:07:38.367 --> 00:07:40.567
-Man, La Schmoove, man.

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:42.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.434
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:44.434 --> 00:07:46.934
Thank you, SantaCon,

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:48.300
for looking like
a "Where's Waldo?"

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.634
for sober people.

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:52.234
It's like, "Oh, that person.
That person."

00:07:52.234 --> 00:07:53.567
[ Applause ]

00:07:57.667 --> 00:08:01.767
Thank you, car reindeer set,
for letting everyone on the road

00:08:01.767 --> 00:08:03.834
know that you're a lot.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.234 --> 00:08:06.701
-Let 'em go.

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:08.067
-Just let 'em go.

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:09.534
Let 'em pass you,
let 'em go the other way,

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:11.334
we don't care, just -- yeah,
they've got something going on.

00:08:11.334 --> 00:08:13.367
-They got some issues.

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:16.634
[ Imitating car horn,
scatting "La Cucaracha" ]

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:21.834
-Thank you, Harry and Meghan's
new Netflix documentary,

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:24.067
for getting King Charles to sign
up for Peacock.

00:08:24.067 --> 00:08:25.133
Ooh, well, there you go.

00:08:25.133 --> 00:08:26.300
That's one way to do it.
[ Chuckles ]

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.501
[ Applause ]

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:30.534
-[ Laughs ]
-[ Chuckles ]

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.033
-Thank you, Spotify Wrapped,
for reminding me

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:38.734
of that one night in May I fell
asleep with whale sounds

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:40.634
on repeat.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:40.634 --> 00:08:43.067
Whale sounds?
That's my song?

00:08:43.067 --> 00:08:44.734
-What?

00:08:44.734 --> 00:08:47.767
-You listened to it
for 1,500 minutes.

00:08:47.767 --> 00:08:49.067
-1,500 minutes of whale sounds.

00:08:49.067 --> 00:08:51.000
Fart noises are number two.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.133
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:57.400
-Thank you, opening one window
while driving,

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.100
for making me feel like
I'm getting an MRI

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.467
in the middle of a tornado.

00:09:00.467 --> 00:09:03.434
It's like...
-[ Warbling sounds ]

00:09:03.434 --> 00:09:05.467
[ Laughs ]

00:09:05.467 --> 00:09:08.667
-Wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-wub-
wub-wub-wub...

00:09:08.667 --> 00:09:11.400
[ Singing "Chariots of Fire" ]
-Make it better, faster,

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.133
stronger.

00:09:13.133 --> 00:09:14.601
-How's everything else going?

00:09:14.601 --> 00:09:17.067
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:18.601
How's that beard coming?

00:09:18.601 --> 00:09:20.300
-It's throwing
the whole game off.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.334
-Yeah.

00:09:21.334 --> 00:09:22.400
-Beard's messing
with your brain.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.200
-It's just making me look, yeah.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.467
-I mean, you never had it,
you know, really properly

00:09:26.467 --> 00:09:28.667
sort of, you know...

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:31.133
-Wow.
-[Crowd] Oh!

00:09:31.133 --> 00:09:32.767
-Wow. Properly sort of?

00:09:32.767 --> 00:09:33.801
-I mean, you know...
-Properly sorted -- that --

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:35.434
-You never had it, like,
you know.

00:09:35.434 --> 00:09:36.634
Like --
-Like what you have?

00:09:36.634 --> 00:09:38.601
-I mean, you could never
have what I have.

00:09:38.601 --> 00:09:39.701
-I don't --
-But, I mean --

00:09:39.701 --> 00:09:41.767
-I don't live in the woods
for eight years.

00:09:41.767 --> 00:09:43.701
[ Laughter ]
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:09:43.701 --> 00:09:45.834
You never had it, like,
you know, connecting and --

00:09:45.834 --> 00:09:48.467
-It looks like you're wearing
a disguise.

00:09:48.467 --> 00:09:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:09:50.901 --> 00:09:52.167
-It's a Brawny paper towel.

00:09:52.167 --> 00:09:54.300
-Yeah, I mean, at least
you can see who it is.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:55.334
-What did Steve say yesterday?

00:09:55.334 --> 00:09:57.534
Your beard looks like
a COVID mask

00:09:57.534 --> 00:09:59.400
with a hole cut out in it?

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:04.601
-He's right!
He's got a point.

00:10:04.601 --> 00:10:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.834 --> 00:10:08.167
It's too thick.

00:10:08.167 --> 00:10:10.501
-Yeah, no.

00:10:10.501 --> 00:10:12.067
-[ Laughs ]
-Thank you,

00:10:12.067 --> 00:10:14.968
office Christmas parties
for having the rule --

00:10:14.968 --> 00:10:16.501
liquor before beer,
you're in the clear.

00:10:16.501 --> 00:10:18.767
Beer before liquor,
you'll see HR quicker.

00:10:18.767 --> 00:10:20.367
There you go, okay.

00:10:20.367 --> 00:10:22.634
There you go.
-"I said that?

00:10:22.634 --> 00:10:23.901
I said that?"

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.267
♪♪

00:10:27.267 --> 00:10:29.000
-Thank you, Aaron Judge,

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.467
or as your family now calls you,
Santa.

00:10:31.467 --> 00:10:32.501
There you have it, everybody.

00:10:32.501 --> 00:10:34.334
Those are our thank-you notes.

00:10:34.334 --> 00:10:37.601
Hey, guys.

00:10:37.601 --> 00:10:40.801
We have exactly six shows left
before we go on Christmas break,

00:10:40.801 --> 00:10:42.067
which means it's time
for that beloved

00:10:42.067 --> 00:10:43.334
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:10:43.334 --> 00:10:46.167
It is time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters"!

00:10:46.167 --> 00:10:47.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:47.334 --> 00:10:49.501
-♪ 12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:10:49.501 --> 00:10:53.367
♪ Six days left ♪

00:10:53.367 --> 00:10:56.434
-That's right, every show
between now and Christmas,

00:10:56.434 --> 00:10:58.601
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:10:58.601 --> 00:11:00.934
a whopper of a Christmas sweater

00:11:00.934 --> 00:11:04.133
from the Countdown to Christmas
Cabinet.

00:11:04.133 --> 00:11:05.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:05.601 --> 00:11:09.701
Since there are six shows left,
let's open door number 6.

00:11:09.701 --> 00:11:11.501
-Ready?
-I'm ready for this.

00:11:11.501 --> 00:11:12.534
-I'm always ready.
-I'm ready.

00:11:12.534 --> 00:11:14.100
-I appreciate this.
-Good. Ready?

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:16.801
[ Drum roll ]

00:11:16.801 --> 00:11:19.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:19.801 --> 00:11:23.234
♪♪

00:11:23.234 --> 00:11:26.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:26.601 --> 00:11:30.901
-I like this one. I like this.

00:11:30.901 --> 00:11:33.267
Flowy.

00:11:33.267 --> 00:11:35.033
Flowy, subtle.

00:11:35.033 --> 00:11:36.501
I like this a lot.

00:11:36.501 --> 00:11:37.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:37.868 --> 00:11:39.734
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:11:39.734 --> 00:11:41.567
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:43.300
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.033
Quest, can I get a drum roll,
please?

00:11:45.033 --> 00:11:50.167
[ Drum roll ]

00:11:50.167 --> 00:11:52.834
2-8-2!

00:11:52.834 --> 00:11:54.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:54.667 --> 00:11:56.868
Yes! Come on, bud.

00:11:56.868 --> 00:12:02.367
♪♪

00:12:02.367 --> 00:12:07.801
♪♪

00:12:07.801 --> 00:12:10.567
Yes, yes, yes!

00:12:10.567 --> 00:12:12.067
Nice to see you, bud.

00:12:12.067 --> 00:12:13.367
How are you?

00:12:13.367 --> 00:12:15.100
Nice to see you, pal.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.534
Congratulations.

00:12:18.534 --> 00:12:20.567
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:12:20.567 --> 00:12:22.334
-Ken Kavanaugh
from Austin, Texas.

00:12:22.334 --> 00:12:23.734
-Yes!

00:12:23.734 --> 00:12:25.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:25.334 --> 00:12:27.934
Austin, Texas.
We love it.

00:12:27.934 --> 00:12:29.501
It does get a little chilly out
there in Texas

00:12:29.501 --> 00:12:30.501
every now and then.

00:12:30.501 --> 00:12:31.701
-Yes, it does.
-Yeah.

00:12:31.701 --> 00:12:32.701
Do you have anything like this
that you could --

00:12:32.701 --> 00:12:33.901
[ Light laughter ]
-No, I do not.

00:12:33.901 --> 00:12:35.100
-No, you don't.
Would you like to try it on

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.501
right now for everyone?

00:12:36.501 --> 00:12:38.868
Speaking about keeping it weird,
we've got to keep it weird,

00:12:38.868 --> 00:12:39.968
Austin.

00:12:39.968 --> 00:12:41.334
♪♪

00:12:41.334 --> 00:12:44.200
Hang on. Here you go.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.234
-Yeah!

00:12:45.234 --> 00:12:46.267
[ Cheering ]

00:12:46.267 --> 00:12:47.567
-Oh, yeah.

00:12:47.567 --> 00:12:48.567
That's perfect.

00:12:48.567 --> 00:12:51.667
Oh! Oh, this is perfect.

00:12:51.667 --> 00:12:52.767
Are you kidding me?

00:12:52.767 --> 00:12:53.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:53.968 --> 00:12:56.567
This is --
that's what you wear out.

00:12:56.567 --> 00:12:58.701
This is fantastic.

00:12:58.701 --> 00:13:00.367
One more time,
give him a round of applause.

00:13:00.367 --> 00:13:01.634
Stick around.
We'll be right back.

00:13:01.634 --> 00:13:03.634
Congratulations.
Happy holidays.

